# Layouts and themes

Every Radii Office app can wear three different looks. They change how the app is arranged, not what it does, and your documents are identical in all of them.

## The three layouts

* {badge Nova | blue | glow} **Nova** is the default. It is flat and soft, with Vadivam icons, rounded corners and a File screen in the same style!
* {badge New | green | soft} **New** is a ribbon like Microsoft Office, with tabs along the top and groups of commands under them!
* {badge Classic | purple | soft} **Classic** is the original look: a glass sidebar with gel buttons, and the page in a bright frame!

## Changing the layout

1. Open the **View** tab (or the **Help** tab in apps without one) and look for **Layout**, or press **Layout** in the ribbon!
2. Pick one of the cards. The app switches right away, and the choice is remembered on this computer!

Some apps have a **Themes** or **Look** button in the sidebar that opens the same cards!

::note Your files do not change
Switching layouts only moves buttons around. Open a document in Classic, switch to Nova, and it is exactly the same file!
::end

## The File screen

The File button (top left in New and Nova, in the sidebar in Classic) opens a full-page screen with the commands that are about the whole file: New, Open, Save a Copy, Export, Print and Info. Which commands appear depends on the app. Cabinet, for example, has Drawers, and Mainkey has Open and Export!

## Poolside layout

Writeout and Bitbook also have a fourth layout, **Poolside**, a glassy look in cyan, blue and orange. It exists only in those two apps!

## Dark and light

Apps follow their layout's colors. This documentation page has its own switch: the moon button at the top right changes between dark and light, and remembers your choice!
